#: src/templates/pages/home.html:136
msgid "What is Codabench?"
msgstr "Codabench 是什么？"

#: src/templates/pages/home.html:139
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Codabench is an <a href=\"%(codabench_repo)s\">open source</a> platform "
"allowing you to organize AI benchmarks. It is flexible and powerful, yet "
"easy to use. You define tasks (e.g. datasets and metrics of success), then "
"interface for submissions of code (algorithms), add some documentation "
"pages, make an upload and that's it! Your benchmark is created, ready to "
"accept submissions of new algorithms. Everything can be fully customized, "
"including the code of the scoring program. Organizers can even hook up their"
" own compute workers to their benchmarks, enabling unlimited computing "
"power. Participants can try out their methods, get real-time feedback and "
"results on a competitive leaderboard, detailed plots and more."
msgstr ""
"Codabench 是一个 <a href=\"%(codabench_repo)s\">开源</a> 平台，帮助你组织 AI "
"基准。它灵活、强大且易于使用。你可以定义任务（例如数据集和评估指标）、配置提交算法的接口、添加文档页面，只需上传即可完成！你的基准会立即生成，准备好接收新的算法提交。所有内容都可以完全自定义，包括评分程序的代码。组织者甚至可以为基准接入自有计算节点，获得无限算力。参赛者可以尝试他们的方法，实时获取反馈和排行榜结果，并查看详细图表等信息。"

#: src/templates/pages/home.html:144
msgid ""
"In a unique twist, Codabench also allows you to create inverted benchmarks. "
"Here, the roles of datasets and algorithms are interchanged. In this "
"scenario, you set the reference algorithms and the participants contribute "
"datasets."
msgstr "更与众不同的是，Codabench 还支持创建反向基准。在这种模式下，数据集和算法的角色互换，你提供参考算法，参赛者提交数据集。"

#: src/templates/pages/home.html:151
msgid "What is CodaLab?"
msgstr "CodaLab 是什么？"

#: src/templates/pages/home.html:154
#, python-format
msgid ""
"CodaLab Competitions is a powerful <a href=\"%(codalab_repo)s\">open "
"source</a> framework for running competitions using result or code "
"submissions. You can participate in an existing competition or host your own"
" competition for free."
msgstr ""
"CodaLab Competitions 是一个功能强大的 <a href=\"%(codalab_repo)s\">开源</a> "
"框架，支持以结果或代码方式提交的竞赛。你可以参加现有竞赛，或免费举办自己的竞赛。"

#: src/templates/pages/home.html:159
msgid ""
"Most competitions hosted on CodaLab are machine learning (data science) "
"competitions, but it is NOT limited to this application domain. It can "
"accommodate any problem for which a solution can be provided in the form of "
"a zip archive containing a number of files to be evaluated quantitatively by"
" a scoring program (provided by the organizers). The scoring program must "
"return a numeric score, which is displayed on a leaderboard where the "
"performances of participants are compared."
msgstr ""
"大多数在 CodaLab 上举办的都是机器学习（数据科学）竞赛，但应用领域并不限于此。只要问题的解可以以包含若干文件的 zip "
"压缩包形式提交，并由主办方提供的评分程序进行量化评估，就能使用 CodaLab。评分程序会返回一个数值分数，显示在排行榜上，以便比较参赛者的表现。"

#: src/templates/pages/home.html:166
msgid "History of CodaLab"
msgstr "CodaLab 的发展历程"

#: src/templates/pages/home.html:169
msgid ""
"CodaLab was created in 2013 as a joint venture between Microsoft and "
"Stanford University. Originally the vision was to create an ecosystem for "
"conducting computational research in a more efficient, reproducible, and "
"collaborative manner, combining worksheets and competitions. Worksheets "
"capture complex research pipelines in a reproducible way and create "
"\"executable papers\". Codabench is the continuity of CodaLab, a version 2 "
"in which users can organize benchmarks."
msgstr ""
"CodaLab 于 2013 "
"年由微软和斯坦福大学联合创建。其愿景是构建一个更高效、可复现、可协作的计算研究生态，将工作表与竞赛结合使用。工作表能够以可复现的方式记录复杂的研究流程，创建“可执行论文”。Codabench"
" 延续了 CodaLab，是让用户组织基准测试的 2.0 版本。"

#: src/templates/pages/home.html:174
#, python-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Some competitions have been organized using worksheets, but the competition "
#| "platform and the worksheet platform have both a large user base and can be "
#| "used independently. In 2014, <a class=\"large_links\" href=\"{{ chalearn_url"
#| " }}\">ChaLearn</a> joined to co-develop CodaLab competitions. Since 2015, "
#| "University Paris-Saclay is community lead of CodaLab competitions, under the"
#| " direction of Isabelle Guyon, professor of big data. CodaLab and Codabench "
#| "are administered by the <a class=\"large_links\" href=\"{{ lisn_url "
#| "}}\">LISN staff.</a>"
msgid ""
"Some competitions have been organized using worksheets, but the competition "
"platform and the worksheet platform have both a large user base and can be "
"used independently. In 2014, <a class=\"large_links\" "
"href=\"%(chalearn_url)s\">ChaLearn</a> joined to co-develop CodaLab "
"competitions. Since 2015, University Paris-Saclay is community lead of "
"CodaLab competitions, under the direction of Isabelle Guyon, professor of "
"big data. CodaLab and Codabench are administered by the <a "
"class=\"large_links\" href=\"%(lisn_url)s\">LISN staff.</a>"
msgstr ""
"部分竞赛通过工作表开展，但竞赛平台和工作表平台各自拥有庞大的用户群，并可独立使用。2014 年，<a class=\"large_links\" "
"href=\"%(chalearn_url)s\">ChaLearn</a> 加入共同开发 CodaLab 竞赛。自 2015 "
"年起，巴黎萨克雷大学在大数据专家 Isabelle Guyon 教授的带领下担任 CodaLab 竞赛的社区负责人。CodaLab 和 "
"Codabench 由 <a class=\"large_links\" href=\"%(lisn_url)s\">LISN 团队</a> 负责运维。"

