#: src/templates/pages/monitor_queues.html:22
msgid ""
"This page allows admins to view connections, queued messages, message rates,"
" channels, exchanges, and other administrative features relating to RabbitMQ"
" e.g. Creating users, adding v-hosts, and creating policies."
msgstr "此页面允许管理员查看 RabbitMQ 的连接、排队消息、消息速率、通道、交换机等管理功能，例如创建用户、添加虚拟主机和配置策略。"

#: src/templates/pages/monitor_queues.html:37
msgid "Flower"
msgstr "Flower"

#: src/templates/pages/monitor_queues.html:39
msgid ""
"Flower is a powerful web-based Celery monitoring tool designed to keep track"
" of our tasks. Admins may view the state of which tasks were run, with what "
"arguments, and many more features. Here you may also view which queues your "
"celery workers are consuming, and the state of any tasks in them. At last, "
"there is also a great monitoring page for viewing the systemic impact of "
"your workers."
msgstr ""
"Flower 是功能强大的 Web 版 Celery 监控工具，可用于跟踪任务执行情况。管理员可以查看已运行任务及其参数等信息，还能看到 Celery "
"worker 正在消费的队列以及其中任务的状态，并通过监控页面了解 worker 对系统的整体影响。"

